FUTURE WORK: ENGAGING THE GENERALIZED KAC–MOODY STRUCTURE

GOAL
  Connect the Monster representation data (valuation table, fusion operator U)
  to the generalized Kac–Moody (GKM) algebras whose denominator formulas
  generate the Moonshine modular functions.

OBJECTS
  M                 : Monster group
  Irr(M)            : irreducible characters {chi_i}
  deg(chi_i)        : chi_i(1)
  v(chi_i)          : valuation vector of deg(chi_i)
  U                 : fusion operator U(x)=F_rho x
  V^natural         : Moonshine VOA
  B                 : Griess algebra = (V^natural)_2
  GKM               : Borcherds generalized Kac–Moody algebra
  Phi(q)            : denominator function of GKM
  T_g(q)            : McKay–Thompson series

DIRECTIONS

1. LIFT REPRESENTATION DATA INTO ROOT MULTIPLICITIES
   Map each Monster irrep chi_i to a candidate root multiplicity m(alpha_i)
   in a Borcherds-type GKM algebra.
   Investigate whether v(chi_i) or Omega(chi_i) can serve as:
     * height functions
     * imaginary root gradings
     * multiplicity weights in the denominator identity.

2. RELATE FUSION OPERATOR U TO GKM CHEVALLEY OPERATORS
   Study U(x)=F_rho x as a discrete analogue of:
     * raising/lowering operators e_alpha, f_alpha
     * imaginary simple root propagation
   Examine whether repeated U-iteration approximates:
     * the automorphic correction process
     * the denominator-product recursion.

3. MATCH VALUATION PROFILES TO MODULAR EXPANSION DATA
   For each prime p in P:
     * compare v_p(chi_i) with the p-adic slopes of T_g(q)
     * test correlations between Omega(chi_i) and q-expansion growth
   Hypothesis:
     valuation mass V_p(x) tracks the same “energy” that appears
     in the modular form’s Fourier coefficients.

4. USE THE CASCADE Γ AS A ROOT-CONSTRUCTION FUNCTOR
   Γ = Pi_VOA o Pi_Griess o Pi_Twist o Pi_Leech o Pi_Golay o Pi_Witt
   Treat Γ as a functor from:
     combinatorial seed → code → lattice → VOA → GKM root data.
   Future work:
     * identify which Γ-layers correspond to real vs. imaginary roots
     * determine how Golay parity and Leech shell structure
       influence the signs in the denominator identity.

5. BUILD A COMPATIBLE HEIGHT FUNCTION
   Define h(chi_i) using:
     * Omega(chi_i)
     * weighted valuation norms
     * Leech shell radii
   Goal:
     produce a height grading compatible with:
       * GKM triangular decomposition
       * Monster module Z-graded structure
       * T_g(q) asymptotics.

6. CONNECT THE TABLE TO THE DENOMINATOR PRODUCT
   The Borcherds denominator has the form:
     Phi(q) = q^{-1} * Π_{n>0} (1 - q^n)^{c(n)}
   Future work:
     * test whether c(n) can be reconstructed from valuation statistics
     * explore whether U-dynamics reproduces the recursive structure
       of c(n) via fusion multiplicities.

7. DEFINE A RELATIONAL FIXED-POINT CONDITION
   Monster symmetry emerges as:
     Aut(V^natural) = Aut(B) = M.
   Future work:
     * express this fixed-point condition inside the GKM algebra
     * identify which roots or imaginary simple roots stabilize
       the valuation table under U.

SUMMARY
  The valuation table is the PED evaluation layer.
  The fusion operator U is the SID dynamical layer.
  The GKM algebra provides the modular layer.
  Future work is to build the bridge:
     valuation → root multiplicity → denominator → modular function.

